--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/team-victory-picture.md
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+# Team victory picture
+
+## Current source composition
+
+The teaser and won-picture branch are now composed on corrected v0.60.9 `628e95daf403082768cdcf900a8ea1d1ef4629a2`, retaining its exact fpv27 bindings and current Settings owner. The lobby remains a concealed border teaser. Both authored arenas have actual-host public-command win/Retry coverage; held artwork must finish behind Settings without taking its selector focus or starting a run. New composed-source test results and browser qualification must be recorded separately before release. No new assets, collision geometry, scoring, saved awards or strict level-format fields are introduced.
+
+## Historical renderer proposal
+
+This scoped P08-A candidate starts from `ece40093940aabdc3b3659a07394b856f33ad4a1` (tree `32b36e6e8fc605911b2cb98cd8f67c97b8f4e214`). It corrects the still-image bridge from a completed Team arena to its accepted picture. It is not phase or public-release acceptance.
+
+## Player-visible change
+
+After First Connection or Relay Yard is won, the Team canvas displays its complete approved picture instead of retaining black concealment and walls. The existing Results dialog remains above the canvas. An unobstructed View Picture action, reveal animation, optional stories and a complete reward journey remain separate P07/P08-B work.
+
+The painter uses the already accepted image lease. Exact level/revision, page snapshot, dimensions, sampling and fit checks still happen before drawing. A won run with a valid image ends its arena paint after that full-frame draw; canvas state is restored. Live hazards, masks, actor bodies and labels no longer cover the won picture. Running, paused and lost arenas retain their current drawing. Procedural or missing-image fallback retains its current path; invalid bindings still refuse rather than silently substituting another image.
+
+This is presentation only. Actual captured cells, coverage, time, reserves, completion events, score and replay behavior are unchanged. The painter does not fetch/decode/dispose images, change registries, award anything or write player progress. A new Retry returns to its normal concealed arena through the existing host.
+
+## Bounded verification
+
+The new complete regression file uses the existing public-command Standard winning routes for both authored arenas. Each actually wins while unclaimed cells remain; Relay Yard also retains authored walls. The real approved PNG bytes pass the existing picture lease validation and a finite decoder. Repeated normal/reduced paints draw the same accepted object in full, with no subsequent concealment or live-arena drawings; state, completion count and resource ownership remain unchanged. Further cases retain running/paused/lost concealment, procedural fallback, rejected image bindings and failed-draw cleanup.
+
+With the exact original renderer, the two authored-win tests fail specifically because later drawing covers the earned picture; the other three new tests pass. The historical renderer candidate passes all **55 tests in four complete files** on both Node 20.19.5 and 22.22.2, sequentially at a 1024 MiB V8 old-space limit. Syntax and formatting checks pass. The 165 fixture inputs are unchanged through each run. Existing picture-binding and actual host files are included; no broad full-suite/build or browser check is claimed.
+
+Cache originals are retained under `.cache/p08a-team-win-picture-ece40093/`, including the original failing output, source preimages, patch, input pins and bounded run receipts. Native rasterization, real winning/result journeys, bright-art contrast, physical controllers/touch, offline/public qualification and full P03/P05/P08-A acceptance remain open. Do not transfer this candidate's results to a later composed source without checking its exact changes.
+
+The lobby does not pre-award this result: its exact prepared original has an opaque black centre and only a narrow border teaser. Tests must pair ready/retained-lobby concealment with the real authored-win renderer, which alone removes the gameplay mask. The teaser changes no progress or image ownership.
